---
import Project from "../../layouts/Project.astro";
---

<Project
  title="Asteroids"
  kind="browser game · coursework project"
  description="A static browser arcade game built with HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and jQuery."
  lead="A keyboard-controlled arcade game built as a web page: dodge asteroids, collect shields, travel through portals, and keep your score climbing as the danger increases."
  links={[
    { label: "Play live game →", href: "https://keeeeeliu.github.io/asteroids-game/", primary: true },
    { label: "Source code →", href: "https://github.com/keeeeeliu/asteroids-game" },
  ]}
  facts={[
    { label: "Type", value: "Static web game" },
    { label: "Year", value: "2024" },
    { label: "Controls", value: "Arrow keys" },
    { label: "Built for", value: "EECS 493" },
    { label: "Status", value: "Ready to deploy separately" },
  ]}
  stack={["HTML", "CSS", "JavaScript", "jQuery", "Sprites", "Audio"]}
>
  <section>
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>
      Asteroids is a single-page browser game. It runs from an <code>index.html</code> file with local
      JavaScript, CSS, image sprites, and sound effects, so it can be deployed as a static site without
      a backend.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Gameplay</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Move the spaceship with the arrow keys</li>
      <li>Dodge animated asteroids that travel across the game window</li>
      <li>Collect shields for temporary protection</li>
      <li>Use portals to advance levels and raise the challenge</li>
      <li>Adjust volume and difficulty before starting</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why it belongs here</h2>
    <p>
      The project is small, but it shows the core mechanics of an interactive web experience:
      keyboard input, collision detection, timed object spawning, score updates, game state transitions,
      and asset-driven animation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Deployment note</h2>
    <p>
      The game itself lives in a separate GitHub repository and is deployed with GitHub Pages, so this
      portfolio page can link out to the playable version without copying the game files into BellaWeb.
    </p>
  </section>
</Project>
